@page
@using MerkaiTrial.Admin.Web.Pages.Quotes
@model MerkaiTrial.Admin.Web.Pages.Quotes.DetailModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = Model.Quote == null ? "Quote" : $"Quote {Model.Quote.Number}";

    var q = Model.Quote;
    var hasExpiry = q != null && DetailModel.HasExpiry(q.ExpiresAtUtc);
    var outWithCustomer = q != null && (q.Status == "Sent" || q.Status == "Viewed");
    var expiryDays = hasExpiry ? Model.DaysUntilExpiry(q!.ExpiresAtUtc) : 0;
    var expiryUrgent = outWithCustomer && hasExpiry && expiryDays <= 3;
    var canInvoice = Model.CanUpdate && Model.UserCanCreate("invoices");
    var moves = Model.StatusActions;
    // q != null first: with no quote loaded IsLocked is false, so without it
    // showDelete could be true and the delete modal would render @q.Number
    // against a null Quote — an NRE on the "quote not found" page.
    var showDelete = q != null && !Model.IsLocked && Model.CanDelete;
}
@* =====================================================================
   Quotes/Detail.cshtml   (029 — rebuild)
   Location: MerkaiTrial.Admin.Web/Pages/Quotes/Detail.cshtml

   COMPLETE FILE — replaces the 018 version.

   WHAT WAS WRONG WITH THE OLD PAGE

   1. IT LOADED BOOTSTRAP AND BOOTSTRAP ICONS AGAIN, from a CDN, inside
      <body>:
          <link href="…/bootstrap@5.3.3/…" rel="stylesheet" />
          <link href="…/bootstrap-icons@1.11.3/…" rel="stylesheet" />
      _Layout.cshtml has already loaded both in <head>. That is two extra
      downloads on every quote, a <link> in an invalid place, and — worse —
      a silent version fork: the day the layout moves to another Bootstrap
      version, this page keeps overriding it with 5.3.3 and nobody knows
      why the buttons look wrong on one page.

   2. ABOUT 340px OF THE SCREEN SAID NOTHING. A 190px purple gradient
      banner reading "Quote Details" (you know — you clicked the quote),
      then up to three stacked alert boxes, then the approval panel, then
      the customer-link box, and only then the quote. On a 768px-tall
      laptop you could not see a single line item without scrolling.
      The banner is gone; the header is one line with the quote number,
      the status and the actions. The three alert boxes are one state
      strip, because only one of them was ever the point.

   3. MONEY WAS SHOWN IN THE WRONG CURRENCY. Every figure went through
      FormatCurrency, which uses the WORKSPACE symbol. A quote raised in
      USD on an Indian workspace printed "₹1,200.00" against dollar
      amounts. Every amount now goes through Model.Money, which uses the
      quote's own currency and prints the ISO code beside the total when
      it is not the workspace currency.

   4. A QUOTE WITH NO EXPIRY DATE PRINTED "01-01-0001". ExpiresAtUtc is a
      non-nullable DateTime; a quote saved without one carries
      default(DateTime) and the page formatted it straight out.

   5. THE PER-LINE DISCOUNT WAS INVISIBLE. The totals showed a Discount
      line, but the item table had no discount column — so a quote with
      ₹40,000 off showed the money vanishing with no explanation of where.

   6. TAX RATES WERE ROUNDED TO WHOLE NUMBERS. (item.TaxRate * 100)
      .ToString("N0") turns a 7.5% rate into "8%".

   7. DELETE ATTACHMENT WAS GATED ON THE WRONG PERMISSION. The button
      checked CanDelete; the handler requires Quotes.Update. So a user
      with Update but not Delete never saw a button the server would have
      accepted, and a user with Delete but not Update saw one that always
      bounced to Access Denied.

   8. "COPY LINK" DID NOTHING ON PLAIN HTTP. navigator.clipboard does not
      exist outside a secure context, so on http:// the handler threw a
      TypeError, the button never changed, and nothing was copied — with
      no error either. There is a fallback now, and the code says when it
      failed.

   9. THE CUSTOMER SAYING NO COULD NOT BE RECORDED. The flow allows
      Sent/Viewed → Rejected and → Expired, but the only button was "Mark
      as Accepted". The status buttons now come from Model.StatusActions,
      which is built from CanChangeStatus, so the page and the flow cannot
      drift apart.

  10. IT WAS UNPRINTABLE. A quote is a document people print or save as
      PDF from the browser. There is a @@media print block now: the nav,
      the buttons and the upload box drop out, and the table prints on
      white.

   TempData alerts are rendered once, globally, by _Layout.cshtml — not
   repeated here. Bootstrap's JS is loaded once by _Layout too.
   ===================================================================== *@

<style>
    .qd { max-width: 1180px; margin: 0 auto; }

    /* ── header ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .qd-back { font-size: .82rem; color: #64748b; text-decoration: none; }
    .qd-back:hover { color: #334155; }
    .qd-head { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin: .35rem 0 1rem; }
    .qd-num { font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; color: #0f172a; line-height: 1.2; margin: 0; }
    .qd-sub { font-size: .84rem; color: #64748b; margin: .2rem 0 0; }
    .qd-acts { display: flex; gap: .45rem; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; }
    .qd-acts form { margin: 0; }

    /* ── state strip ────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .qd-state { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: .75rem; flex-wrap: wrap;
                border: 1px solid #e9ecef; border-left: 5px solid var(--tone, #94a3b8);
                border-radius: 10px; background: #fff; padding: .7rem 1rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
    .qd-state .txt { font-size: .88rem; color: #334155; }
    .qd-state .txt strong { color: #0f172a; }
    .qd-state .sp { margin-left: auto; }

    /* ── panels ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .qd-card { border: 1px solid #e9ecef; border-radius: 12px; background: #fff; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
    .qd-card > h2 { font-size: .8rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .05em; color: #64748b;
                    font-weight: 650; margin: 0; padding: .7rem 1rem; border-bottom: 1px solid #f1f3f5;
                    display: flex; align-items: center; gap: .4rem; }
    .qd-card > h2 .badge { font-weight: 650; }
    .qd-card .bd { padding: .9rem 1rem; }
    .qd-card .bd.flush { padding: 0; }

    /* ── facts ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .qd-facts { display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto 1fr; gap: .4rem .9rem; font-size: .86rem; }
    .qd-facts dt { color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 500; }
    .qd-facts dd { margin: 0; color: #0f172a; min-width: 0; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }

    /* ── line items ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .qd-items { width: 100%; border-collapse: separate; border-spacing: 0; font-size: .86rem; }
    .qd-items th { font-size: .7rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .05em; color: #64748b;
                   font-weight: 650; padding: .55rem .75rem; background: #fbfcfd;
                   border-bottom: 1px solid #eceff2; white-space: nowrap; }
    .qd-items td { padding: .6rem .75rem; border-bottom: 1px solid #f4f6f8; vertical-align: top; }
    .qd-items tbody tr:last-child td { border-bottom: 0; }
    .qd-items .n { text-align: right; white-space: nowrap; }
    .qd-items .c { text-align: center; white-space: nowrap; }
    .qd-items .nm { font-weight: 600; color: #0f172a; }
    .qd-items .ds { color: #64748b; font-size: .8rem; margin-top: .15rem; }
    .qd-items .muted { color: #94a3b8; }

    /* ── totals ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .qd-tot { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto; gap: .35rem .9rem; font-size: .88rem; }
    .qd-tot .lbl { color: #64748b; }
    .qd-tot .amt { text-align: right; font-weight: 600; white-space: nowrap; }
    .qd-tot .rule { grid-column: 1 / -1; border-top: 1px solid #e5e8ec; margin: .35rem 0 .1rem; }
    .qd-tot .big { font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 700; color: #0f172a; }
    .qd-fx { font-size: .74rem; color: #94a3b8; margin-top: .5rem; }

    /* ── customer link ──────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .qd-link code { display: block; background: #f1f5f9; color: #1e40af; border-radius: 6px;
                    padding: .45rem .6rem; font-size: .78rem; word-break: break-all; margin: .4rem 0 .5rem; }

    /* ── attachments ────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .qd-att { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: .6rem; padding: .6rem 1rem;
              border-bottom: 1px solid #f4f6f8; }
    .qd-att:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
    .qd-att .ico { font-size: 1.3rem; color: #94a3b8; flex: 0 0 auto; }
    .qd-att .nm { font-weight: 600; font-size: .84rem; color: #0f172a; }
    .qd-att .mt { font-size: .74rem; color: #94a3b8; }
    .qd-att .btns { margin-left: auto; display: flex; gap: .25rem; flex: 0 0 auto; }
    .qd-att .btns .btn { --bs-btn-padding-y: .15rem; --bs-btn-padding-x: .45rem; }

    .qd-empty { padding: 1.4rem 1rem; text-align: center; color: #94a3b8; font-size: .84rem; }

    @@media (max-width: 767.98px) {
        .qd-num { font-size: 1.25rem; }
        .qd-acts { width: 100%; }
        .qd-acts > *, .qd-acts form { flex: 1 1 calc(50% - .25rem); }
        .qd-acts .btn { width: 100%; }
        .qd-facts { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0 0; }
        .qd-facts dt { margin-top: .5rem; font-size: .74rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .04em; }
    }

    /* ── print ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    /* A quote gets printed and saved as PDF from the browser. Strip the
       chrome and anything you cannot act on from paper. */
    @@media print {
        .qd { max-width: none; }
        .qd-back, .qd-acts, .qd-noprint, .qap, nav, header, footer,
        aside, .navbar, .sidebar { display: none !important; }
        .qd-card { border: 1px solid #ccc; break-inside: avoid; margin-bottom: .6rem; }
        .qd-state { border: 1px solid #ccc; }
        a[href]:after { content: ""; }
        body { background: #fff !important; }
    }
</style>

@* Two sibling blocks rather than an early `return;` inside the body: a
   bare return in a Razor page compiles, but it is the kind of thing that
   breaks on a Razor version bump, and a build break here costs a lot more
   than one extra @@if. *@
@if (q == null)
{
    <div class="qd">
        <div class="qd-card">
            <div class="qd-empty">
                <i class="bi bi-file-earmark-x d-block mb-2" style="font-size:2.2rem;color:#d7dde3;"></i>
                <div class="fw-semibold text-body mb-1">Quote not found</div>
                <div>It may have been deleted. <a asp-page="/Quotes/Index">Back to quotes</a>.</div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
}
else
{
<div class="qd">

    <a asp-page="/Quotes/Index" class="qd-back">
        <i class="bi bi-arrow-left me-1"></i>All quotes
    </a>

    @* ── header ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
    <div class="qd-head">
        <div style="min-width:0;">
            <h1 class="qd-num">@q.Number</h1>
            <p class="qd-sub">
                <span class="badge @Model.GetStatusBadgeClass(q.Status)">
                    <i class="bi @DetailModel.StatusIcon(q.Status) me-1"></i>@DetailModel.StatusLabel(q.Status)
                </span>
                <span class="ms-1">@q.CompanyName</span>
                @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(q.DealTitle))
                {
                    <span class="text-muted">· @q.DealTitle</span>
                }
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="qd-acts ms-auto">
            @* Status moves, from Model.StatusActions — already filtered through
               CanChangeStatus, so this list and the workflow cannot drift. *@
            @foreach (var m in moves)
            {
                <form method="post" asp-page-handler="UpdateStatus" asp-route-id="@Model.Id"
                      class="qd-move" data-confirm="@m.Confirm">
                    <input type="hidden" name="newStatus" value="@m.Status" />
                    <button type="submit" class="btn btn-sm @m.Css">
                        <i class="bi @m.Icon me-1"></i>@m.Label
                    </button>
                </form>
            }

            @* PDF — reading is enough, so this shows for a locked quote too.
               rel="noopener" because target="_blank" without it hands the new
               tab a window.opener reference to this page. *@
            <a asp-page="/Quotes/Detail" asp-page-handler="DownloadPdf" asp-route-id="@Model.Id"
               class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                <i class="bi bi-file-earmark-pdf me-1"></i>PDF
            </a>

            @if (!Model.IsLocked && Model.CanUpdate && Model.IsEditableStatus)
            {
                <a asp-page="/Quotes/Edit" asp-route-id="@Model.Id" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary">
                    <i class="bi bi-pencil me-1"></i>Edit
                </a>
            }

            @if (showDelete)
            {
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-danger"
                        data-bs-toggle="modal" data-bs-target="#qdDeleteModal">
                    <i class="bi bi-trash me-1"></i>Delete
                </button>
            }

            @if (Model.IsLocked)
            {
                <span class="badge bg-info-subtle text-info-emphasis border border-info-subtle px-2 py-2">
                    <i class="bi bi-lock-fill me-1"></i>
                    @(Model.Invoice != null ? "Invoiced — view only" : "Closed — view only")
                </span>
            }
        </div>
    </div>

    @* ── state strip ────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
    @* ONE strip, not three stacked alerts. Which one you get is decided by
       priority: a live invoice outranks "accepted, raise an invoice",
       which outranks the plain status hint. *@
    @if (Model.Invoice != null)
    {
        <div class="qd-state" style="--tone:#0d6efd;">
            <i class="bi bi-receipt" style="font-size:1.1rem;color:#0d6efd;"></i>
            <span class="txt">
                @if (Model.InvoiceIsDraft)
                {
                    <text><strong>A draft invoice exists</strong> for this quote — check the dates, then issue it to give it a number.</text>
                }
                else
                {
                    <text>Invoiced as <strong>@Model.Invoice.Number</strong>.</text>
                }
            </span>
            <a href="/Invoices/Detail?id=@Model.Invoice.Id" class="btn btn-sm btn-primary sp qd-noprint">
                @(Model.InvoiceIsDraft ? "Open draft" : "View invoice")
                <i class="bi bi-arrow-right ms-1"></i>
            </a>
        </div>
    }
    else if (q.Status == "Accepted")
    {
        <div class="qd-state" style="--tone:#198754;">
            <i class="bi bi-check-circle-fill" style="font-size:1.1rem;color:#198754;"></i>
            <span class="txt">
                @* The old page promised "You can now create an invoice" to
                   everybody, including a rep with read-only Invoices who had
                   no button to press. The promise matches the button. *@
                @if (canInvoice)
                {
                    <text><strong>The customer accepted.</strong> Raise an invoice from it when you're ready.</text>
                    @if (Model.VoidInvoiceCount > 0)
                    {
                        <text> The previous invoice was voided.</text>
                    }
                }
                else
                {
                    <text><strong>The customer accepted this quote.</strong></text>
                }
            </span>
            @if (canInvoice)
            {
                <form method="post" asp-page-handler="CreateInvoice" asp-route-id="@Model.Id"
                      class="sp qd-noprint">
                    <button type="submit" class="btn btn-sm btn-success">
                        <i class="bi bi-receipt-cutoff me-1"></i>Create invoice
                    </button>
                </form>
            }
        </div>
    }
    else if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(Model.StatusHint))
    {
        var tone = q.Status switch
        {
            "PendingApproval" => "#ffc107",
            "Approved"        => "#20c997",
            "Sent"            => "#0d6efd",
            "Viewed"          => "#0dcaf0",
            "Rejected"        => "#dc3545",
            "Expired"         => "#fd7e14",
            "Revised"         => "#6c757d",
            _                 => "#94a3b8"
        };

        <div class="qd-state" style="--tone:@tone;">
            <i class="bi @DetailModel.StatusIcon(q.Status)" style="font-size:1.1rem;color:@tone;"></i>
            <span class="txt">@Model.StatusHint</span>
            @if (expiryUrgent)
            {
                <span class="sp badge @(expiryDays < 0 ? "bg-danger" : "bg-warning text-dark")">
                    <i class="bi bi-hourglass-split me-1"></i>@Model.ExpiryNote(q.ExpiresAtUtc)
                </span>
            }
        </div>
    }

    @* (017) Approval panel — draws nothing when there's nothing to say *@
    <partial name="_QuoteApprovalPanel" model="Model" />

    <div class="row g-3">

        @* ── LEFT: line items + totals ──────────────────────────── *@
        <div class="col-lg-8">

            <div class="qd-card">
                <h2>
                    <i class="bi bi-list-ul"></i>Line items
                    <span class="badge bg-light text-dark border ms-1">@q.Items.Count</span>
                </h2>
                <div class="bd flush">
                    <div class="table-responsive">
                        <table class="qd-items">
                            <thead>
                                <tr>
                                    <th style="width:2.2rem;">#</th>
                                    <th>Item</th>
                                    <th class="c">Qty</th>
                                    <th class="n">Unit price</th>
                                    @* NEW. The totals show a Discount line; without this
                                       column the money came off with no explanation. *@
                                    <th class="n">Discount</th>
                                    <th class="n">Tax</th>
                                    <th class="n">Line total</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                @if (q.Items.Count == 0)
                                {
                                    <tr>
                                        <td colspan="7" class="qd-empty">
                                            This quote has no line items, so its total is zero.
                                            @if (Model.CanUpdate && Model.IsEditableStatus)
                                            {
                                                <a asp-page="/Quotes/Edit" asp-route-id="@Model.Id">Add some</a><text>.</text>
                                            }
                                        </td>
                                    </tr>
                                }
                                @for (var i = 0; i < q.Items.Count; i++)
                                {
                                    var it = q.Items[i];
                                    <tr>
                                        <td class="muted">@(i + 1)</td>
                                        <td>
                                            <div class="nm">@it.Name</div>
                                            @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(it.Description))
                                            {
                                                <div class="ds">@it.Description</div>
                                            }
                                        </td>
                                        <td class="c">@it.Quantity</td>
                                        <td class="n">@Model.Money(it.UnitPrice)</td>
                                        <td class="n @(it.LineDiscount > 0 ? "" : "muted")">
                                            @(it.LineDiscount > 0 ? "−" + Model.Money(it.LineDiscount) : "—")
                                        </td>
                                        @* TaxRate on the DTO is a FRACTION (0.18 = 18%), unlike
                                           QuoteItemData on the Create/Edit pages where it is a
                                           percentage. "0.##" instead of "N0" so a 7.5% rate stops
                                           printing as 8%. *@
                                        <td class="n muted">@((it.TaxRate * 100).ToString("0.##"))%</td>
                                        <td class="n fw-semibold">@Model.Money(it.LineGrandTotal)</td>
                                    </tr>
                                }
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="qd-card">
                <h2><i class="bi bi-calculator"></i>Totals</h2>
                <div class="bd">
                    <div class="row justify-content-end">
                        <div class="col-sm-8 col-md-7">
                            <div class="qd-tot">
                                <div class="lbl">Subtotal</div>
                                <div class="amt">@Model.Money(q.Subtotal)</div>

                                <div class="lbl">Discount</div>
                                <div class="amt @(q.DiscountTotal > 0 ? "text-success" : "")">
                                    @(q.DiscountTotal > 0 ? "−" + Model.Money(q.DiscountTotal) : Model.Money(0))
                                </div>

                                <div class="lbl">Tax</div>
                                <div class="amt">@Model.Money(q.TaxTotal)</div>

                                <div class="rule"></div>

                                <div class="lbl big">Grand total</div>
                                <div class="amt big">@Model.Money(q.GrandTotal)</div>
                            </div>

                            @* Spelled out whenever the quote is priced in something
                               other than the workspace currency — the case the old
                               page silently mislabelled with the workspace symbol. *@
                            @if (Model.QuoteInForeignCurrency)
                            {
                                <div class="qd-fx">
                                    <i class="bi bi-info-circle me-1"></i>
                                    Priced in <strong>@q.Currency</strong>, not your workspace currency
                                    (@Model.CurrencyCode). No conversion is applied.
                                </div>
                            }
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        @* ── RIGHT: facts, link, attachments ────────────────────── *@
        <div class="col-lg-4">

            <div class="qd-card">
                <h2><i class="bi bi-info-circle"></i>Details</h2>
                <div class="bd">
                    <dl class="qd-facts">
                        <dt>Company</dt>
                        <dd>@q.CompanyName</dd>

                        <dt>Deal</dt>
                        <dd>@(string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(q.DealTitle) ? "—" : q.DealTitle)</dd>

                        @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(q.VerticalName))
                        {
                            <dt>Industry</dt>
                            <dd>@q.VerticalName</dd>
                        }

                        <dt>Issued</dt>
                        <dd>@Model.FormatDate(q.IssueDateUtc)</dd>

                        <dt>Expires</dt>
                        <dd>
                            @if (hasExpiry)
                            {
                                @Model.FormatDate(q.ExpiresAtUtc)
                                @if (outWithCustomer)
                                {
                                    <span class="d-block @(expiryDays < 0 ? "text-danger fw-semibold" : expiryDays <= 3 ? "text-warning-emphasis fw-semibold" : "text-muted")"
                                          style="font-size:.78rem;">
                                        @Model.ExpiryNote(q.ExpiresAtUtc)
                                    </span>
                                }
                            }
                            else
                            {
                                @* The old page printed 01-01-0001 here. *@
                                <span class="text-muted">Not set</span>
                            }
                        </dd>

                        <dt>Currency</dt>
                        <dd>@(string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(q.Currency) ? Model.CurrencyCode : q.Currency)</dd>

                        <dt>Created</dt>
                        <dd>@Model.FormatDate(q.CreatedAtUtc)</dd>
                    </dl>
                </div>
            </div>

            @* Customer link — only exists once the quote has gone out *@
            @if (outWithCustomer && !string.IsNullOrEmpty(q.PaymentLinkUrl))
            {
                <div class="qd-card qd-link qd-noprint">
                    <h2>
                        <i class="bi bi-link-45deg"></i>Customer link
                        @if (q.Status == "Viewed")
                        {
                            <span class="badge bg-success-subtle text-success-emphasis border border-success-subtle ms-auto">
                                <i class="bi bi-eye-fill me-1"></i>Opened
                            </span>
                        }
                    </h2>
                    <div class="bd">
                        <div class="text-muted" style="font-size:.8rem;">
                            Send by email, LINE or WhatsApp. The customer can view and accept it online.
                        </div>
                        <code id="qdLink">@q.PaymentLinkUrl</code>
                        <div class="d-flex gap-2 flex-wrap">
                            <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary" id="qdCopy">
                                <i class="bi bi-clipboard me-1"></i>Copy link
                            </button>
                            <a href="@q.PaymentLinkUrl" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
                               class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary">
                                <i class="bi bi-box-arrow-up-right me-1"></i>Preview
                            </a>
                        </div>
                        <div class="text-danger mt-2 d-none" id="qdCopyFail" style="font-size:.78rem;">
                            Couldn't copy automatically — select the link above and copy it by hand.
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            }

            <div class="qd-card">
                <h2>
                    <i class="bi bi-paperclip"></i>Attachments
                    <span class="badge bg-light text-dark border ms-1">@Model.Attachments.Count</span>
                </h2>

                @* The UPLOAD form and the DELETE button are both gated on
                   CanUpdate, because OnPostUploadAttachment and
                   OnPostDeleteAttachment both call
                   ValidatePermissionAsync(Actions.Update). Delete used to be
                   gated on CanDelete, which disagreed with its own handler in
                   both directions. *@
                @if (Model.CanUpdate)
                {
                    <div class="bd border-bottom qd-noprint">
                        <form method="post" asp-page-handler="UploadAttachment" asp-route-id="@Model.Id"
                              enctype="multipart/form-data">
                            <div class="input-group input-group-sm">
                                <input type="file" name="file" class="form-control" required
                                       accept=".pdf,.doc,.docx,.xls,.xlsx,.jpg,.jpeg,.png,.gif,.webp,.txt,.csv" />
                                <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">
                                    <i class="bi bi-upload"></i>
                                </button>
                            </div>
                            <div class="text-muted mt-1" style="font-size:.74rem;">
                                PDF, Word, Excel, images, CSV — up to 10 MB
                            </div>
                        </form>
                    </div>
                }

                <div class="bd flush">
                    @if (!Model.Attachments.Any())
                    {
                        <div class="qd-empty">Nothing attached yet.</div>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        @foreach (var att in Model.Attachments)
                        {
                            <div class="qd-att">
                                <i class="bi @att.FileIcon ico"></i>
                                <div style="min-width:0;">
                                    <div class="nm text-truncate" title="@att.FileName">@att.FileName</div>
                                    <div class="mt">
                                        @att.FileSizeDisplay · @Model.FormatDateTime(att.CreatedAtUtc)
                                        @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(att.CreatedBy))
                                        {
                                            <text> · @att.CreatedBy</text>
                                        }
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="btns qd-noprint">
                                    <a href="@att.FileUrl" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
                                       class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary" title="Download @att.FileName">
                                        <i class="bi bi-download"></i>
                                    </a>
                                    @if (Model.CanUpdate)
                                    {
                                        @* The file name goes in a data- attribute, never into an
                                           inline onsubmit string: Razor encodes an apostrophe in
                                           "Client's brief.pdf" to &#x27;, the parser decodes it
                                           before the JS is parsed, and the handler becomes a
                                           syntax error. A throwing onsubmit does not return
                                           false, so the form would submit and delete the file
                                           without asking. *@
                                        <form method="post" asp-page-handler="DeleteAttachment"
                                              asp-route-id="@Model.Id" asp-route-attachmentId="@att.Id"
                                              class="qd-attdel" data-name="@att.FileName">
                                            <button type="submit" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-danger"
                                                    title="Delete @att.FileName">
                                                <i class="bi bi-trash"></i>
                                            </button>
                                        </form>
                                    }
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        }
                    }
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
}

@* Delete modal — rendered only when the button that opens it exists.
   The old page emitted it for every quote, including locked ones where it
   had no Delete button in its footer at all. *@
@if (showDelete)
{
    <div class="modal fade" id="qdDeleteModal" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true" aria-labelledby="qdDeleteTitle">
        <div class="modal-dialog modal-dialog-centered">
            <div class="modal-content">
                <div class="modal-header">
                    <h5 class="modal-title" id="qdDeleteTitle">
                        <i class="bi bi-exclamation-triangle text-danger me-2"></i>Delete this quote?
                    </h5>
                    <button type="button" class="btn-close" data-bs-dismiss="modal" aria-label="Close"></button>
                </div>
                <div class="modal-body">
                    <p class="mb-1 fw-semibold">@q.Number — @q.DealTitle</p>
                    <p class="text-muted small mb-0">
                        @q.Items.Count line @(q.Items.Count == 1 ? "item" : "items"),
                        @Model.Money(q.GrandTotal). This cannot be undone.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="modal-footer">
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" data-bs-dismiss="modal">Cancel</button>
                    <form method="post" asp-page-handler="Delete" asp-route-id="@Model.Id" class="d-inline">
                        <button type="submit" class="btn btn-danger">
                            <i class="bi bi-trash me-1"></i>Delete quote
                        </button>
                    </form>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
}

@* Bootstrap JS is already loaded once by _Layout.cshtml — not loaded again.
   Alert auto-dismiss is handled globally by _Layout too. *@
<script>
    (function () {
        'use strict';

        // ── 1. copy the customer link ────────────────────────────────
        // navigator.clipboard does NOT exist outside a secure context, so on
        // plain http:// the old handler threw a TypeError and the button just
        // sat there. Try the modern API, fall back to a hidden textarea, and
        // say so when neither works.
        var copyBtn = document.getElementById('qdCopy');
        var linkEl = document.getElementById('qdLink');
        var failEl = document.getElementById('qdCopyFail');

        function flash(ok) {
            if (!copyBtn) return;
            if (!ok) { if (failEl) failEl.classList.remove('d-none'); return; }
            if (failEl) failEl.classList.add('d-none');

            var original = copyBtn.innerHTML;
            copyBtn.innerHTML = '<i class="bi bi-check2 me-1"></i>Copied';
            copyBtn.classList.remove('btn-outline-primary');
            copyBtn.classList.add('btn-success');
            setTimeout(function () {
                copyBtn.innerHTML = original;
                copyBtn.classList.remove('btn-success');
                copyBtn.classList.add('btn-outline-primary');
            }, 1800);
        }

        function legacyCopy(text) {
            try {
                var ta = document.createElement('textarea');
                ta.value = text;
                ta.setAttribute('readonly', '');
                ta.style.position = 'fixed';
                ta.style.top = '-1000px';
                document.body.appendChild(ta);
                ta.select();
                var ok = document.execCommand('copy');
                document.body.removeChild(ta);
                return ok;
            } catch (e) {
                return false;
            }
        }

        if (copyBtn && linkEl) {
            copyBtn.addEventListener('click', function () {
                var text = (linkEl.textContent || '').trim();
                if (!text) return;

                if (navigator.clipboard && window.isSecureContext) {
                    navigator.clipboard.writeText(text)
                        .then(function () { flash(true); })
                        .catch(function () { flash(legacyCopy(text)); });
                } else {
                    flash(legacyCopy(text));
                }
            });
        }

        // ── 2. confirmations, from data- attributes ──────────────────
        // One delegated listener for both the status moves and the attachment
        // deletes. Nothing is interpolated into a JS string, so a quote number
        // or a file name containing an apostrophe cannot break the handler.
        document.addEventListener('submit', function (e) {
            var form = e.target;
            if (!form || !form.classList) return;

            if (form.classList.contains('qd-move')) {
                var msg = form.getAttribute('data-confirm');
                if (msg && !window.confirm(msg)) e.preventDefault();
                return;
            }

            if (form.classList.contains('qd-attdel')) {
                var name = form.getAttribute('data-name') || 'this file';
                if (!window.confirm('Delete ' + name + '? This cannot be undone.')) e.preventDefault();
            }
        });
    })();
</script>
